From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 13:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Match swapchain candidates to activation ownership

Lineage II keeps its game VkSurface across fullscreen transitions, while
Purple On leaves a newer, inactive graphics-probe surface on the same HWND.
Destroying the game's old swapchain temporarily assigns ownership to that
inactive surface.

The candidate query only accepts the current owner or the newest registered
surface, so the game gets a locally retired background swapchain. Activation
then picks the game as the newest active surface. commit_client_swapchain()
rejects the owner mismatch and deactivation restores the inactive probe as
owner. Every retry repeats this cycle with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR, leaving
a fullscreen window without game contents.

Predict the same newest-active selection that activation will make, treating
the queried surface as active without changing its counters. Only a newer
active surface can disqualify it. Preserve creation order, active replacement
priority, and the commit-time check for genuine concurrent ownership changes.

This corrects the candidate predicate added by the background-presenter
coordination patch; it does not remove that coordination or change the
fullscreen policy.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -4565,8 +4565,17 @@
 static BOOL wayland_client_surface_is_presentation_candidate(
         struct wayland_win_data *data, struct wayland_client_surface *surface)
 {
-    return data->client_surface == surface ||
-           wayland_client_surface_find_owner(data, NULL, FALSE) == surface;
+    struct wayland_client_surface *candidate;
+
+    /* Predict find_owner(active_only) after activating this surface. Newer
+     * inactive surfaces, including graphics probes, must not block it. */
+    LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY_REV(candidate, &data->client_surfaces,
+                            struct wayland_client_surface, hwnd_entry)
+    {
+        if (candidate == surface) return TRUE;
+        if (ReadAcquire(&candidate->client.active_ref)) return FALSE;
+    }
+    return FALSE;
 }
 
 /* Presentation ownership follows graphics-surface creation order. Replacement
